    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0962" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2402a: Circular Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Diplomatic
                        Representatives in Certain Latin American Countries</hi><anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d783-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-15T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1921—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>By instruction of the President of the United States, the Military Governor of
                    Santo Domingo issued today<anchor n="17" xml:id="d783-f2"/> a proclamation
                    addressed to the Dominican people, in substance as follows:</p>
                <pb facs="0963" n="839" xml:id="pg839"/>
                <p>[Here follows the substance of the proclamation printed on <ref target="#pg835"
                        >page 835</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Secure publication of this summary in all leading newspapers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d783-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d783-f1-content">
                <p>To those in Argentina, Bolivia, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Cuba, Ecuador, Panama,
                    Paraguay, Peru, Uruguay, and Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d783-f2" n="17" xml:id="d783-f2-content">
                <p>The proclamation was issued June 14.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
